From 9ea0575c67a1dd3153a65528f5fe8e17a01ebbcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:10:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update-pause): a long context compression yields to a
 core-update pause [daveey]

A Desktop turn in a post-tool compression held its admission reservation
unpublished until the summary ended (hub 2026-11-12: 302 s, so the instant
apply came 306 s past due): a pause lands only at a step boundary and the
mid-tool cancel tracked tool calls only.

The compression host wait now registers with agent.update_pause_cancel as an
in-flight call. After the same MID_TOOL_GRACE_S the watcher's cancel makes the
wait fence-cancel the summary before its commit and return the unchanged
transcript (no stall fallback, no timeout cooldown); the turn then pauses at
the next step boundary and releases its reservation. An admitted commit still
completes. The host-wait helpers move to conversation_compression_wait.py
(re-exported) to keep conversation_compression.py under its line cap.

Task: t_01a1d0aa52ee1404
